    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW29V3UomkqehSCVSRkTj1Bkq)_\n\n## What\nFollow-up to #355 (it merged before this last commit was pushed). #355 flags crossref chains deeper than two levels and skips them; this adds the individual command to convert one anyway.\n- New `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill-deep-chain`, run in the flagged note:\n  - it refuses a note whose chain is not deep (use `sp-litnotes-meta-fill`)\n  - it shows the chain (`ch -> b -> c`) and asks once\n  - it fills the note and links or makes its direct parent\n  - the parent is filled by the normal rules (`sp-litnotes-meta--allow-chain` is off for it), so a loop is cut there and the grandparent is made only when the parent's chain is no deeper\n- No batch version: each deep chain is converted by hand.\n- The dry run section \"Crossref chains deeper than two levels\" now points to the command.\n- Literate doc updated as bullet lists; it tangles to the committed `.el`.\n\n## Tests\n- 37 tests in `tests/sp-litnotes-meta-test.el` pass in Emacs 29; new ones: declined, converted (makes `b` then `c`), loop cut at the parent, refuses a normal note.\n- Not run on the real vault or in Emacs 31.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits, per the nightly-tidy rule.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiD5W4k4UTcudsexBjX)_",
